cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this material, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "大模型的小练习（三）：朗顿蚂蚁在 n×n 棋盘上的逃逸时间上界"
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-11-26"
authors:
  - name: "yutitan"
repository-code: "https://github.com/yutitan/langton-ant-square-bound"
url: "https://github.com/yutitan/langton-ant-square-bound"
abstract: >-
  An explicit escape-time bound for Langton's ant on n x n boards:
  S(n) <= 730*(9/5)^n for every n >= 1. The proof is computer-assisted:
  20 locally impossible heading fragments compress the history into a
  108-state automaton, 171 rational gain inequalities are checked exactly,
  and an analytic range bound gives the global constant. The repository
  contains the verification programs, an independent audit script and a
  full proof note.
keywords:
  - Langton's ant
  - cellular automata
  - escape time
  - computer-assisted proof
  - AI-assisted exploration
license: MIT
notes: >-
  Series: 大模型的小练习（三） (LLM Exercises III); the first entry is
  https://github.com/yutitan/wowii-conjecture-138 and the second is
  https://github.com/yutitan/langton-ant-three-rows. Derived with GPT 6.2
  Astra (OpenAI Codex, model gpt-6.2-astra) on 2026-11-26 and independently
  verified with DeepSeek Harness. This is a public record of a personal
  AI-assisted exploration and makes no priority claim. The comparison with
  Etse (MFCS 2026) and Ke's preprint is as stated by the model and was not
  independently checked.
